From: rtw89-usb-ap-fix <local@patch>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 11:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rtw89: extend RTL8922A DACK RFK wait for USB

RTL8922AU firmware RFK reports can arrive far later over USB than the
PCIe-oriented 58 ms DACK wait used by RTL8922A.  On iStoreOS/RPi4 this
prints "failed to wait RF DACK" during AP bring-up and leaves the
following RFK sequence racing a still-running DACK calibration.

Use a USB-specific DACK wait window.  Other RFK waits keep their
upstream values so failed C2H paths do not make every channel change
block for a long time.
---
 phy.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/phy.c b/phy.c
--- a/phy.c
+++ b/phy.c
@@ -4190,6 +4190,9 @@ int rtw89_phy_rfk_dack_and_wait(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev,
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	if (rtwdev->hci.type == RTW89_HCI_TYPE_USB)
+		ms = max(ms * 1000, 60000U);
+
 	rtw89_phy_rfk_report_prep(rtwdev);
 
 	ret = rtw89_fw_h2c_rf_dack(rtwdev, phy_idx, chan);
